      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David, when he fled from Saul in the cave. Be merciful to me, O God, be merciful to me: for my soul trusteth in thee: yes, in the shadow of thy wings will I make my refuge, until ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " calamities are overpast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.57.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.57.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will cry to God most high; to God that performeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "all things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.57.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.57.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall send from heaven, and save me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the reproach of him that would swallow me up. Selah. God shall send forth his mercy and his truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
